 Persons who are generally unable to lead a normal
life due to physical, mental, or cognitive problems
are called persons with disabilities or special
needs. According to the Rights and Protection of
Persons with Disabilities Act, 2013, ‘Person with
Disability’ means a congenital/long -term or
permanent physical, mental, intellectual,
developmental or sensory impairment or
disadvantage of a person and the interaction of
attitude and environmental barriers due to which
the person concerned is prevented from
participating fully and effectively in society on an
equal basis. Note that if a person has autism,
physical, mental, vision, speech, intelligence,
hearing, cerebral palsy, down syndrome, and other
disabilities, he is considered disabled or ha ving
special needs.
